    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10360" root="خرط" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَرَّاطٌ</span></b>  <i>One whose occupation is to remove the
bark,</i> or <i>peel, of wood,</i> or <i>sticks, and to plane it,</i>
or <i>make it even,</i> (K,) <i>with the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِخْرَط</span>, which is
also called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلْط</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُلْط</span>, (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بلط</span>,) or
<i>with the hand.</i> (TA in the present art.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[Hence, in modern Arabic, <i>A turner</i> of wood &amp;c.]


